Third-party binaries redistributed with this project
===================================================

`aobs` itself is licensed under `LICENSE`. This file is about the binaries the **input archive**
carries, because those are what a release redistributes.

What is redistributed
---------------------

`aobs-inputs-vMAJOR.MINOR.tar`, published as a release asset, carries:

- the **appliance apk closure** and the **toolchain apk closure** — Alpine Linux `.apk` packages,
  **unmodified**, exactly as Alpine published them, with their upstream signatures intact;
- Alpine's **verbatim** `APKINDEX.tar.gz` for `main` and `community`;
- `alpine-minirootfs-<version>-x86_64.tar.gz`, Alpine's own release tarball;
- `linux-<version>.tar.xz`, the vanilla kernel.org source tarball.

That the packages are unmodified is not a promise, it is a consequence: `build/mkiso.sh` installs
them without `--allow-untrusted`, which is only possible because neither the packages nor Alpine's
own index was regenerated here. A rebuilt index is refused as `UNTRUSTED signature`.

Licences
--------

Several of the packages are under the GPL — busybox, kbd and grub among them. **The per-package
licence, origin aport and aports git commit are recorded in the `NOTICE` file inside the archive
itself**, generated from Alpine's own metadata by `build/apkindex.py`, so the record travels with
the bytes rather than living only in a file a redistributor may not have kept.

The manifest's `aports-commit:` field names one commit as a pointer — the aports recipe commit of
`alpine-release`, the branch's release-marker package. The complete per-package record is the
archive's own `NOTICE`.

Written offer
-------------

The corresponding build recipes for each redistributed package are those in the Alpine aports tree
<https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports> at the commit named for that package in the archive's
`NOTICE`.

**Buildable upstream sources are explicitly not promised.** Alpine's distfiles retention is
unverified and plausibly as lossy as its `.apk` retention — the CDN keeps only the current version of
each package, confirmed against 7/7 official mirrors, with no archive host in existence. A claim that
the sources remain downloadable is a claim nobody has checked, and this project does not make claims
of that kind. What the recorded commits do guarantee is **locatable recipes in a history that does not
expire.**

Vendored source
---------------

Two libraries are vendored into the application tree as source, not as binaries, and carry their own
licences beside them:

- `aobs/core/vendor/embit/` — see `aobs/core/vendor/embit/LICENSE`
- `aobs/core/vendor/ur2/` — see `aobs/core/vendor/ur2/LICENSE`

`aobs/core/vendor/README.md` records which upstream commit each was taken from and why they are
vendored rather than installed. No binary artifact is present in either tree, and
`build/verify.py`'s `check_vendored_tree` fails the build if one appears.
